ENTRY            G4123   20261010   20261124   20261124       G061
SUBENT        G4123001   20261010   20261124   20261124       G061
BIB                 15         38
TITLE      Study of the 67Cu activation in (gamma,p)-reaction at
           Ebr=19 MeV
AUTHOR     (V.O.Zheltonozhsky,D.E.Myznikov,A.M.Savrasov,
           V.I.Slisenko, N.V.Kulich)
INSTITUTE  (4UKRIJD)
REFERENCE  (J,YFE,27,213,2026)
           #doi:10.15407/jnpae2026.03.213
FACILITY   (MICRT,4UKRIEP) The M-30 microtron
INC-SOURCE (BRST)
METHOD     (ACTIV) Induced gamma-activity was measured.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) The spectra were measured by two gamma
           spectrometers assembled on the basis of HPGe
           detectors from Canberra and Ortec. The energy
           resolution of both spectrometers was 1.9 keV on the
           gamma-line at 1332 keV, which accompanies the 60Co
           decay. The detection efficiency of the spectrometers
           was determined using the standard 152,154Eu and 133Ba
           calibration point sources.
SAMPLE     To monitor the flow of bremsstrahlung gamma-quanta,
           samples of natural metallic tantalum with a thickness
           of 15 mu-m and gold with a thickness of 10 mu-m were
           used. During irradiation, a target of metallic zinc
           of natural isotopic composition with a mass of 570 mg
           and dimensions close to the sizes of the monitoring
           targets was added to them.
ADD-RES    Experimental data are compared with theoretical
           predictions calculated with TALYS-1.96 code.
MONITOR    (73-TA-181(G,N)73-TA-180,,SIG,,BRA)
           (79-AU-197(G,N)79-AU-196,,SIG,,BRA)
MONIT-REF  (,V.V.Varlamov+,J,PAN,76,1403,2013)
           (L0021003,A.Veyssiere+,J,NP/A,159,561,1970)
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) The total error of the experimental
           flux-weighted average yields was within 9%, the
           dominant uncertainty being the monitor flux-weighted
           average yield of the 181Ta(gamma,n)180Ta and
           197Au(gamma,n)196Au reactions.
STATUS     (TABLE,,V.O.Zheltonozhsky+,J,YFE,27,213,2026) Page 217.
